# Third-party notices

PitWall Desktop original code is MIT-licensed (see [LICENSE](LICENSE)). This file
records third-party software and marks that the project redistributes, links
against, or refers to. Exact license texts ship with each package on crates.io,
npm, or the upstream repository.

## Generating dependency inventories

```powershell
npm run gen:notice
```

That writes `NOTICE.generated.md` (gitignored inventory). Maintainers should
refresh and merge relevant lines into this file before each tagged release.

Policy: Rust licenses are enforced by [`deny.toml`](deny.toml) (`cargo deny`).
npm licenses are enforced by `npm run check:licenses`. Engineering guidance:
[docs/IP.md](docs/IP.md).

